                <pb facs="0984" n="874" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg874"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">352.1153 St 2/106: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hammond</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Sebastian</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-09-05T12:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 5,
                                1928—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 10:55 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>82. Department’s 54, August 30, 1 p.m. French Embassy intends to continue
                    pressing for increased compensation for good will, with <pb facs="0985" n="875"
                        xml:id="pg875"/> the hint that unless some increase is forthcoming they will
                    invoke arbitration under their treaty. The question is now dormant and French
                    Embassy does not expect to take any action before end of October.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hammond</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
